MAME ctlsock: an absolute ioport field needs no accumulator, no cursor
readback and no dead reckoning -- state it directly.

WHY

Every existing pointer route the ctlsock module drives (MOVEA's closed-loop
convergence via cursor-register readback, or its open-loop dead-reckoning
fallback; the abs-ram route that pokes a guest's low-memory mouse globals) is
built for a RELATIVE input device: a guest reads a delta and integrates it
itself, or keeps its own belief of the pointer in RAM the module can read
back and correct against.

Palm OS's pen digitizer is neither. MAME's palm.cpp models it as two true
absolute analog ioport fields -- IPT_LIGHTGUN_X/Y, PORT_MINMAX(0,0xa0) -- plus
a digital "Pen Button" whose PORT_CHANGED_MEMBER latches whatever the X/Y
fields currently read. The field's CURRENT VALUE *is* the pen position; there
is no delta to integrate and no on-screen cursor sprite to read back and
converge against (there is no cursor at all -- the pen either touches or it
doesn't). Every existing route either does nothing (no cursor items exist to
read) or actively fights the guest (an accumulator's running total gets
clamped to 0..0xa0 by set_value() on the very first write past a few counts,
so the pen never reaches most of the digitizer).

WHAT IT ADDS

  MAME_CTL_ABS   1 => MOVEA writes m_x_field/m_y_field DIRECTLY, scaled from
                 the published surface (MAME_CTL_SCREEN) into each field's
                 own PORT_MINMAX range (read via ioport_field::minval()/
                 maxval(), so nothing here is Palm-specific)   [unset]

Applies AFTER mame-ctlsock.patch and mame-ctlsock-ptr-tags.patch (the two
patches that bind m_x_field/m_y_field and parse MAME_CTL_SCREEN into
m_surf_w/m_surf_h -- this patch only adds the short-circuit in movea_target()
that fires when MAME_CTL_ABS is set and both fields are bound).

CONTAINMENT

Unset reproduces every existing caller byte for byte: m_abs_fields defaults
false, and the new branch in movea_target() is a no-op until MAME_CTL_ABS=1
AND both ptr-tags fields are bound. No save items are added, so the
savestate signature is unchanged and no golden is orphaned.

It also carries the ABSOLUTE AXIS BINDING fallback. ptr-tags binds the axis
handles by matching IPT_MOUSE_X/Y, which no absolute-axis machine has, so
before this patch m_x_field/m_y_field stayed null on exactly the machines
MAME_CTL_ABS exists for -- every MOVEA acked OK while the pen never left its
power-on centre (MEASURED on palmpro, 2026-09-20). The fallback is gated on
MAME_CTL_ABS and only ever fills a handle that would otherwise be null, so it
is inert for every existing station.

MEASURED: see docs/lab/PALMOS-WAVE.md for the palmpro five-target pointer
proof this patch made possible.

--- a/src/osd/modules/ctlsock/ctlsock.cpp
+++ b/src/osd/modules/ctlsock/ctlsock.cpp
@@ -416,6 +416,16 @@
 			m_btn_name[1] = "Right Button";
 			m_btn_name[2] = "Middle Button";
 		}
+		// Absolute-field bind: some machines (Palm's IPT_LIGHTGUN_X/Y pen
+		// digitizer) expose the pointer as a true absolute analog ioport
+		// field, not a relative counter a guest driver differences. For
+		// those MAME_CTL_ABS=1 makes MOVEA write the target directly into
+		// the already-bound m_x_field/m_y_field (scaled from the published
+		// surface into the field's own PORT_MINMAX range via minval()/
+		// maxval()) instead of running the dead-reckoning engine above --
+		// there is no cursor register to read back and nothing to converge.
+		// Unset reproduces every existing caller unchanged.
+		m_abs_fields = env_long("MAME_CTL_ABS", 0) != 0;
 		m_cursor_items = env_str("MAME_CTL_CURSOR_ITEMS");
 		m_swap_items = env_str("MAME_CTL_SWAP_ITEMS");
 		m_tail_path = env_str("MAME_CTL_CMD_FILE");
@@ -1021,6 +1031,25 @@
 			for (ioport_field &f : m_y_port->fields())
 				if (f.type() == IPT_MOUSE_Y)
 					m_y_field = &f;
+		// ABSOLUTE AXIS FALLBACK. The type match above looks for a RELATIVE
+		// mouse counter (IPT_MOUSE_X/Y). A machine whose pointer is a true
+		// absolute analog axis -- Palm's pen digitizer is IPT_LIGHTGUN_X/Y,
+		// PORT_MINMAX(0,0xa0) -- has no such field, so both handles stayed
+		// null and MAME_CTL_ABS's direct write below could never fire:
+		// MEASURED on palmpro 2026-09-20, the pen never left its 0x50,0x50
+		// power-on centre while every MOVEA still acked OK.
+		// Deliberately a FALLBACK and deliberately gated on MAME_CTL_ABS: it
+		// can only bind a handle that would otherwise be null, on a station
+		// that has explicitly asked for the absolute route, so it is inert
+		// for every existing caller.
+		if (m_abs_fields && m_x_port && !m_x_field)
+			for (ioport_field &f : m_x_port->fields())
+				if (f.type() == IPT_LIGHTGUN_X)
+					m_x_field = &f;
+		if (m_abs_fields && m_y_port && !m_y_field)
+			for (ioport_field &f : m_y_port->fields())
+				if (f.type() == IPT_LIGHTGUN_Y)
+					m_y_field = &f;
 
 		// MOVEA's SENSOR: raw handles onto the hardware-cursor registers
 		// (on irix: the Newport VC2's m_cursor_x/y — upstream save items
@@ -1872,6 +1901,25 @@
 	{
 		x = std::max(0L, std::min(m_surf_w - 1, x));
 		y = std::max(0L, std::min(m_surf_h - 1, y));
+
+		if (m_abs_fields && m_x_field && m_y_field)
+		{
+			// direct absolute write: the published pixel maps linearly onto
+			// each field's own declared range (e.g. Palm's Pen X/Y, 0..0xa0),
+			// no accumulator, no cursor readback, no dead reckoning -- this
+			// machine's pointer field IS the position, not a delta of it.
+			long const fx_max = long(m_x_field->maxval());
+			long const fy_max = long(m_y_field->maxval());
+			long const fx = (m_surf_w > 1) ? std::lround(double(x) * fx_max / double(m_surf_w - 1)) : 0;
+			long const fy = (m_surf_h > 1) ? std::lround(double(y) * fy_max / double(m_surf_h - 1)) : 0;
+			m_x_field->set_value(u32(fx));
+			m_y_field->set_value(u32(fy));
+			trace("verb MOVEA(abs) seq=%s tgt=%d,%d field=%d,%d", seq, int(x), int(y), int(fx), int(fy));
+			hist_apply(ack);
+			reply_ok(ack);
+			return;
+		}
+
 		hist_apply(ack);
 		reply_ok(ack);  // MOVEA acks on target-accept; completion is EV MOVEA
 		trace("verb MOVEA seq=%s tgt=%d,%d", seq, int(x), int(y));
@@ -3110,6 +3158,7 @@
 	ioport_field *m_btn_field[3] = { nullptr, nullptr, nullptr };
 	ioport_field *m_x_field = nullptr;
 	ioport_field *m_y_field = nullptr;
+	bool m_abs_fields = false;               // MAME_CTL_ABS: direct field write, no dead reckoning
 	std::unordered_map<std::string, ioport_port *> m_port_cache;
 
 	long m_mx = 0, m_my = 0;                 // pointer accumulators (seed rules above)
